asr-000087
00:44:13.360 --> 00:44:14.980
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Good morning to everyone.

asr-000088
00:44:18.330 --> 00:44:20.410
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: To our Department of Agriculture family,

asr-000089
00:44:21.470 --> 00:44:26.070
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: led by Secretary Francisco Kiko Tiu Laurel Jr.,

asr-000090
00:44:26.070 --> 00:44:29.630
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: in the National Irrigation Administration family,

asr-000091
00:44:29.630 --> 00:44:33.990
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: led by Administrator Eduardo Eddie Guillen,

asr-000092
00:44:35.170 --> 00:44:38.950
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: our partners from the Civil Society Organization

asr-000093
00:44:38.950 --> 00:44:44.450
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and all colleagues participating in today's budget hearing,

asr-000094
00:44:44.850 --> 00:44:45.430
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: good morning.

asr-000095
00:44:47.520 --> 00:44:52.100
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Today, our task is not merely to review our profession,

asr-000096
00:44:53.160 --> 00:44:57.260
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: but to support in sharpening the agri-sector's direction,

asr-000097
00:44:57.260 --> 00:44:59.540
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: raise local production,

asr-000098
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:04.080
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: improve the incomes of farmers and peasant folks,

asr-000099
00:45:04.740 --> 00:45:13.380
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and ensure that assistance reaches producers in the right place and at the right time.

asr-000100
00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:19.670
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: As President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. reminded us,

asr-000101
00:45:20.730 --> 00:45:26.410
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: our national budget serves as our moral and economic compass,

asr-000102
00:45:26.410 --> 00:45:33.150
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: always pointing toward making life better for our people.

asr-000103
00:45:34.670 --> 00:45:47.530
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The fiscal year 2027 NEP proposes P198.45 billion for the DA in its attached corporations,

asr-000104
00:45:47.530 --> 00:45:56.090
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: while P46.36 billion is proposed as budgetary support

asr-000105
00:45:56.090 --> 00:45:56.390
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: for the DA in its attached corporations.

asr-000106
00:45:56.410 --> 00:46:09.000
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We support the Department's direction to treat these resources as one value-chain strategy,

asr-000107
00:46:10.080 --> 00:46:18.420
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: from land, water, credit, and mechanized production to poor harvest facilities,

asr-000108
00:46:19.220 --> 00:46:24.620
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: logistic, market matching, and better return for producers.

asr-000109
00:46:24.620 --> 00:46:27.620
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The P16 billion program,

asr-000110
00:46:27.660 --> 00:46:29.800
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the Farm-to-Market Road Program,

asr-000111
00:46:30.720 --> 00:46:33.880
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the P250 million CADIWA program,

asr-000112
00:46:35.040 --> 00:46:36.640
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: cold storage facilities,

asr-000113
00:46:37.660 --> 00:46:38.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: consolidation,

asr-000114
00:46:38.360 --> 00:46:43.860
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and digital market information should work together

asr-000115
00:46:43.860 --> 00:46:48.660
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: to reduce transport costs and spoilage,

asr-000116
00:46:48.880 --> 00:46:51.200
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: improve farm gate prices,

asr-000117
00:46:52.040 --> 00:46:56.760
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and connect farmers and peasant folks with reliable buyers.

asr-000118
00:46:59.540 --> 00:47:03.900
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: And because water is the lifeblood of our field,

asr-000119
00:47:05.260 --> 00:47:15.380
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the fiscal year 2027 NEP proposes P46.36 billion in budgetary support for NIA,

asr-000120
00:47:15.380 --> 00:47:22.960
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: with only 2.20 million hectares developed out of the country,

asr-000121
00:47:23.700 --> 00:47:29.120
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: 3.13 million hectares of potential irrigatable area,

asr-000122
00:47:29.540 --> 00:47:30.300
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and more than 1.5 million hectares of land.

asr-000123
00:47:30.300 --> 00:47:38.160
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We support NIA's direction to accelerate irrigation development

asr-000124
00:47:38.160 --> 00:47:42.840
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: while giving equal attention to refer restoration,

asr-000125
00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:47.960
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: climate adoption, and service road improvements,

asr-000126
00:47:48.900 --> 00:47:53.120
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: irrigation, funding, and projects should be coordinated

asr-000127
00:47:53.120 --> 00:47:56.120
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: with the DA community plans,

asr-000128
00:47:56.120 --> 00:48:01.120
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: crops, calendars, LGUs, and irrigation.

asr-000129
00:48:01.340 --> 00:48:13.980
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We also support NIA's commitment to improve the quality of the water and the environment

asr-000130
00:48:13.980 --> 00:48:14.040
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: so that every new or restored system immediately support additional production in diversified cropping.

asr-000131
00:48:15.420 --> 00:48:22.060
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Production support must also include timely and affordable agricultural credit,

asr-000132
00:48:22.800 --> 00:48:25.380
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: particularly for small farmers,

asr-000133
00:48:26.240 --> 00:48:30.480
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: peasant folks, cooperatives, and farmers' associations.

asr-000134
00:48:31.340 --> 00:48:36.040
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Mechanization through PELMIG in the DA Banners Program

asr-000135
00:48:36.040 --> 00:48:40.900
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: must improve labor and output efficiency,

asr-000136
00:48:41.900 --> 00:48:48.440
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: expand harvesting, drying, storage, and processing capacity,

asr-000137
00:48:48.440 --> 00:48:53.540
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and reduce losses between harvest and market credit.

asr-000138
00:48:54.400 --> 00:49:00.580
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Equipment, training, insurance, and market access should be delivered,

asr-000139
00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:08.760
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: as an integrated package in coordination with LGUs and local farmers

asr-000140
00:49:08.760 --> 00:49:12.500
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: rather than as separate interventions.

asr-000141
00:49:13.860 --> 00:49:18.860
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Every allocation proposed for the year 2027

asr-000142
00:49:18.860 --> 00:49:23.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: must be authored on a clear purpose,

asr-000143
00:49:23.340 --> 00:49:28.900
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: a defined intervention in a missionable result.

asr-000144
00:49:29.800 --> 00:49:31.320
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We must be able to explain,

asr-000145
00:49:31.340 --> 00:49:34.920
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: not only how much we are requesting,

asr-000146
00:49:35.580 --> 00:49:37.620
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: but why we are requesting it,

asr-000147
00:49:38.500 --> 00:49:41.220
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: what problem it addresses,

asr-000148
00:49:42.220 --> 00:49:44.780
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: who will benefit in what improvement.

asr-000149
00:49:45.520 --> 00:49:50.660
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We expect to see where program have demonstrated results.

asr-000150
00:49:51.460 --> 00:49:56.920
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We must identify how to sustain our scale of this gain,

asr-000151
00:49:56.920 --> 00:50:01.320
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: where implementation challenges have been increased,

asr-000152
00:50:01.340 --> 00:50:03.140
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: why it's being considered,

asr-000153
00:50:03.140 --> 00:50:04.180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and how to be the key to the improvement.

asr-000154
00:50:04.180 --> 00:50:06.160
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: This must be addressed through better planning,

asr-000155
00:50:06.160 --> 00:50:10.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: stronger education, and more program design.

asr-000156
00:50:11.520 --> 00:50:13.480
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Our objective is clear,

asr-000157
00:50:14.100 --> 00:50:18.620
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: to arrive at a budget proposal that is credible,

asr-000158
00:50:19.500 --> 00:50:22.660
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: responsive performance informed,

asr-000159
00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:27.380
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and capable of delivering meaningful results

asr-000160
00:50:27.380 --> 00:50:29.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: for the Philippines agriculture.

asr-000161
00:50:30.140 --> 00:50:30.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Accordingly,

asr-000162
00:50:30.340 --> 00:50:31.320
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: I hope that the government of the Philippines will provide us with a number of means for developing a more robust and sustainable program.

asr-000163
00:50:31.340 --> 00:50:57.100
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The committee will look for clear regional and community targets, accessible credit, operational irrigation system, lower post-harvest losses, stronger market, matching, and better day-to-day coordination that gives local farmers a direct voice in planning and implementation.

asr-000164
00:50:57.100 --> 00:51:17.180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: At this point, before the agencies begin their representation, I would like to introduce the sponsor of today's budget, Vice Chairman Dr. Anna York, our lead sponsor.

asr-000165
00:51:18.440 --> 00:51:28.540
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Congressman York cannot join us physically as he is attending the needs of our constituents in Pampanga, which until now may baha pa po doon.

asr-000166
00:51:28.760 --> 00:51:41.540
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Of course, your trolleys, Congressman Bong Tebes, and the sponsor of NIA budget, Vice Chairman Joseph Tan.

asr-000167
00:51:42.860 --> 00:51:54.640
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: With that, I welcome everyone today for Fiscal Year 2027 Department of Culture and National Irrigation Administration Budget Hearing.

asr-000168
00:51:54.640 --> 00:51:59.640
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: We look forward to support today in NIA moving these reforms toward...

asr-000169
00:52:00.780 --> 00:52:05.280
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: ...a more productive, efficient, and resilient agricultural sector.

asr-000170
00:52:05.880 --> 00:52:08.920
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you, and I wish everyone a productive discussion.

asr-000171
00:52:09.600 --> 00:52:15.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Mr. Chairman, Mr. Chairman, Rufus Rodriguez here, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000172
00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:20.420
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: May I raise a point of inquiry?

asr-000173
00:52:21.460 --> 00:52:30.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The budget hearing schedule promulgated by the Committee on Appropriations has two agencies at the same time, 1030,

asr-000174
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:31.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: which is the DA...

asr-000175
00:52:32.660 --> 00:52:38.780
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: ...with Secretary Benitez, and NIA, with Administrator Guillen.

asr-000176
00:52:39.580 --> 00:52:47.660
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: May I know whether this will be successive or it will be joined at the same time, and we will be given 10 minutes each?

asr-000177
00:52:52.730 --> 00:52:53.950
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Joined in 10 minutes.

asr-000178
00:52:54.230 --> 00:52:56.010
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Five minutes each.

asr-000179
00:52:56.250 --> 00:52:58.730
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay, thank you very much. Five minutes each.

asr-000180
00:52:59.010 --> 00:53:04.010
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we'll all be able to ask five minutes to the DA, five minutes to the NIA.

asr-000181
00:53:05.010 --> 00:53:06.650
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you for that ruling, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000182
00:53:06.950 --> 00:53:13.170
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The clarification: five minutes, joint NIA and DA.

asr-000183
00:53:13.390 --> 00:53:19.090
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Oh, I thought that it will be separate because many here, like me, I have combined.

asr-000184
00:53:20.730 --> 00:53:22.390
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Oh, mahirap yun.

asr-000185
00:53:23.070 --> 00:53:28.270
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because I have many questions. There are many agencies in the DA and I have many questions.

asr-000186
00:53:28.690 --> 00:53:33.110
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And then with NIA, I have also questions because I got zero in the NEP in NIA.

asr-000187
00:53:34.170 --> 00:53:34.650
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Zero.

asr-000188
00:53:35.410 --> 00:53:35.890
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Butlog.

asr-000189
00:53:36.950 --> 00:53:37.450
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: In Bisaya.

asr-000190
00:53:38.110 --> 00:53:38.810
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Neil, Nada.

asr-000191
00:53:39.630 --> 00:53:40.150
Committee member: Mr. Chair.

asr-000192
00:53:40.730 --> 00:53:49.390
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, may we know whether we should add some more minutes because five minutes will not be sufficient for both big agencies of government with separate budgets.

asr-000193
00:53:51.230 --> 00:53:54.530
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: May we know what will be the consideration of the Chair?

asr-000194
00:53:57.020 --> 00:53:57.520
Committee member: Mr. Chair.

asr-000195
00:53:57.520 --> 00:54:00.280
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: I think, siguro, flexible na lang tayo.

asr-000196
00:54:00.540 --> 00:54:07.900
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: But anyway, there will be a consultation on Thursday, September 3, for DA.

asr-000197
00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:18.180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: That's why, yung inyong mga parang keyal concern, pwede niyong ma-address doon during consultation sa DA this coming Thursday.

asr-000198
00:54:18.180 --> 00:54:29.060
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: But, boss, siguro, flexible na lang natin kung lalampas tayo ng five minutes.

asr-000199
00:54:29.800 --> 00:54:31.180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Siguro, hindi ko na...

asr-000200
00:54:31.900 --> 00:54:37.200
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: But anyway, ang rules po na natin is for five minutes.

asr-000201
00:54:37.640 --> 00:54:38.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you for that.

asr-000202
00:54:38.380 --> 00:54:38.880
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And flexibility.

asr-000203
00:54:39.700 --> 00:54:42.980
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I hope when Kaganyoro speaks, we'll be given another five minutes.

asr-000204
00:54:43.220 --> 00:54:43.540
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-000205
00:54:44.160 --> 00:54:44.820
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you.

asr-000206
00:54:45.460 --> 00:54:46.020
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Mr. Chairman.

asr-000207
00:54:47.080 --> 00:54:47.580
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Mr. Chair.

asr-000208
00:54:48.360 --> 00:54:48.620
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: May I?

asr-000209
00:54:50.120 --> 00:54:50.820
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Mr. Chair.

asr-000210
00:54:52.500 --> 00:54:53.700
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Congressman, your witness.

asr-000211
00:54:54.520 --> 00:54:55.680
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000212
00:54:55.680 --> 00:55:00.140
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: I joined the manifestation of Honorable Rodriguez, Mr. Chair.

asr-000213
00:55:00.760 --> 00:55:08.360
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: In fact, this representation also had so many concerns, not only on the DA, but more particularly on the NIA.

asr-000214
00:55:08.380 --> 00:55:13.320
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: So, I think more than five minutes is enough for us, Mr. Chair.

asr-000215
00:55:14.380 --> 00:55:15.160
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you.

asr-000216
00:55:17.420 --> 00:55:30.940
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: And then, before the day of presentation, let us hear from the Vice Chair Bundok, my co-lead for her message.

asr-000217
00:55:32.920 --> 00:55:38.540
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much, Pong Tevez and Vice Chair Tevez.

asr-000218
00:55:38.660 --> 00:55:40.680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much, everyone, and good morning.

asr-000219
00:55:40.680 --> 00:55:42.480
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I hope you can hear me.

asr-000220
00:55:43.240 --> 00:55:44.600
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Good morning, everyone.

asr-000221
00:55:44.840 --> 00:56:00.040
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I am the Vice Chair in charge of the Department of Agriculture, and I am pleased to welcome everyone to our consultation and budget presentation of the Department of Agriculture for the 2027 budget.

asr-000222
00:56:00.740 --> 00:56:12.060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Unfortunately, I cannot join you and cannot be physically present today because of severe and persistent flooding in Central Luzon, Pampanga, and most especially in my district.

asr-000223
00:56:12.280 --> 00:56:12.880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yes.

asr-000224
00:56:13.240 --> 00:56:28.900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The San Simon-Enlex exit, which has now caused a 10-hour backlog and a Carmageddon, which is causing problems not only for our district, but for the entire Metro Manila and the entire north, is in my district also.

asr-000225
00:56:29.460 --> 00:56:32.580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nevertheless, I am honored to welcome everyone today.

asr-000226
00:56:33.340 --> 00:56:40.940
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much to Secretary Francisco Kiko Tiu Laurel Jr. of the Department of Agriculture and to the DA family.

asr-000227
00:56:40.940 --> 00:56:42.620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And thank you also.

asr-000228
00:56:43.240 --> 00:56:50.180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I would like to recognize our NIA Administrator, Admin Eduardo Eddie-Guillen today.

asr-000229
00:56:50.660 --> 00:57:02.700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: To my colleagues who are taking over for me today, Congressman Joseph Tan, who is representing the NIA, Vice Chair Pong Tevez, and also Vice Chair Christopher Gua.

asr-000230
00:57:02.780 --> 00:57:05.980
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much for assisting me during these difficult times.

asr-000231
00:57:06.860 --> 00:57:11.740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nevertheless, we are here today to address so many issues facing the DA.

asr-000232
00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:13.080
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Number one of them is…

asr-000233
00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:13.120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Number one of which is...

asr-000234
00:57:13.120 --> 00:57:13.220
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Number one of which is…

asr-000235
00:57:13.240 --> 00:57:21.580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: which is food security, the stability of food prices, the welfare of farmers, support for our economy.

asr-000236
00:57:22.400 --> 00:57:26.600
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And I think one of the most important issues today is recovery from the flood,

asr-000237
00:57:27.020 --> 00:57:29.900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: which is the worst flood which has ever occurred in the Philippines,

asr-000238
00:57:30.240 --> 00:57:35.360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and sadly has occurred in the rice granary of the Philippines, Central Luzon.

asr-000239
00:57:35.360 --> 00:57:39.040
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And of course, we must face the challenges of climate change,

asr-000240
00:57:39.040 --> 00:57:46.020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: which is one of the major causes of the El Nino flood, which is ravaging Philippine agriculture today.

asr-000241
00:57:46.800 --> 00:57:54.680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Together with the DA family and the NIA, we welcome your concerns and will try to address them accordingly.

asr-000242
00:57:56.670 --> 00:58:00.170
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you for your questions and we will work together with you,

asr-000243
00:58:00.170 --> 00:58:09.830
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: hopefully to a successful support for the 2027 budget of the Department of Agriculture and the National Irrigation Authority.

asr-000244
00:58:10.290 --> 00:58:14.030
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So thank you so much, everyone. Maya Payabak po, and good morning.

asr-000245
00:58:16.990 --> 00:58:18.950
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you, Vice-Chair Bundok.

asr-000246
00:58:21.640 --> 00:58:27.080
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Secretary Laurel, you may now proceed with your presentation.

asr-000247
00:58:29.340 --> 00:58:34.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Honorable members of Congress, distinguished colleagues, ladies and gentlemen,

asr-000248
00:58:34.060 --> 00:58:36.020
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: good morning to all.

asr-000249
00:58:37.220 --> 00:58:42.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We are here today to present the Department of Agriculture's proposed budget for fiscal year 2027

asr-000250
00:58:42.580 --> 00:58:44.300
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: and to seek the continued support of the Department of Agriculture and the National Irrigation Authority.

asr-000251
00:58:44.300 --> 00:58:55.160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: The President emphasized in his budget message,

asr-000252
00:58:55.680 --> 00:58:59.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: the national budget must ultimately make a difference in the lives of our people.

asr-000253
00:59:00.140 --> 00:59:06.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: For the Department of Agriculture, that means two things that are inseparable,

asr-000254
00:59:07.500 --> 00:59:11.660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ensuring that the Filipino families have sufficient, safe, nutritious, and affordable food,

asr-000255
00:59:11.660 --> 00:59:14.280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: and making sure that farmers and fisher folks,

asr-000256
00:59:14.300 --> 00:59:18.300
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: who produce that food, can earn a decent and sustainable living.

asr-000257
00:59:18.300 --> 00:59:20.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We cannot have one without the other.

asr-000258
00:59:20.800 --> 00:59:26.600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We cannot demand affordable food while leaving those who produce it struggling to cover their costs.

asr-000259
00:59:26.600 --> 00:59:31.100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And we cannot expect our farmers and fisher folks to keep producing for the nation

asr-000260
00:59:31.100 --> 00:59:38.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: if farming and fishing no longer provide them with a viable livelihood and a better life for their families.

asr-000261
00:59:38.800 --> 00:59:43.100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: This is why agriculture must be properly and sufficiently funded.

asr-000262
00:59:43.100 --> 00:59:48.400
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Every investment we make in agriculture is, at its core, an investment in food security.

asr-000263
00:59:48.940 --> 00:59:51.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: It is an investment in the people who put food on our tables,

asr-000264
00:59:52.360 --> 00:59:54.500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: and it is an investment in the future of our country.

asr-000265
00:59:55.400 --> 00:59:58.760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Our farmers and fisher folk continue to face high production costs,

asr-000266
00:59:58.760 --> 00:59:59.980
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: changing weather,

asr-000267
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:06.240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: patterns climate related risks market uncertainties and other challenges that can quickly turn

asr-000268
01:00:06.240 --> 01:00:12.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: a good harvest or a good catch into a difficult year yet despite these challenges we must

asr-000269
01:00:12.800 --> 01:00:19.520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: continue to ensure that food reaches filipino families in sufficient supply and at prices that

asr-000270
01:00:19.520 --> 01:00:26.640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: they can afford our proposed 2027 budget is designed to help bridge that gap we will continue

asr-000271
01:00:26.640 --> 01:00:32.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: investing in programs that will raise productivity improve farm and fishery infrastructure reduce

asr-000272
01:00:32.800 --> 01:00:38.480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: post-harvest losses strengthen logistics and market access and expand the use of appropriate

asr-000273
01:00:38.480 --> 01:00:43.760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: technologies we will strengthen agriculture and fisheries value change so that the farmers and

asr-000274
01:00:43.760 --> 01:00:50.160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: fisher folk can capture greater share of the value they create we will also continue building

asr-000275
01:00:50.160 --> 01:00:56.320
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: a sector that's more resilient to climate change disasters market disruptions and other risks

asr-000276
01:00:57.600 --> 01:01:02.880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: in a moment our undersecretary for finance undersecretary nora c oliveras will present

asr-000277
01:01:02.880 --> 01:01:07.600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: the details of our proposed budget and the programs and investments behind these priorities

asr-000278
01:01:08.320 --> 01:01:12.240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: but beyond the numbers we must always ask what these investments will deliver

asr-000279
01:01:13.520 --> 01:01:18.320
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: mga katulong baang ma eto upang higit na dumami ang produksyon at lumaki ang kita ng ating mga

asr-000280
01:01:18.320 --> 01:01:25.520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: magsasaka at manging isda makakabawas baang ma eto sa pagkaluget makapaghatid ng pagkain sa

asr-000281
01:01:26.640 --> 01:01:33.440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pangmahalikan ng mas mabilis at mas mahusay makapagbibigay ba ang ma eto ng mga mas

asr-000282
01:01:33.440 --> 01:01:39.600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: matatag sapat nigtas at abot kayang supply ng pagkain para sa sambayanan at higit sa lahat

asr-000283
01:01:39.600 --> 01:01:46.240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: mga katulong baang ma eto upang magkaroon ng maas maayos at mas manangal na buhay ang mga taong

asr-000284
01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:52.640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: araw-araw na nagsisikap upang may pagkain sa ating mga hapag ito ang mga kongkretong resulta na

asr-000285
01:01:52.640 --> 01:01:54.880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: dapat nating sama-samang pagsikapang makamit

asr-000286
01:01:56.640 --> 01:02:01.440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na rin ng kagawaran na ang bawat pisong ipagkakatiwala sa atin ay pera ng taong bayan

asr-000287
01:02:01.440 --> 01:02:10.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: kaya dapat itong gamitin ng wasto maingat mahusay at may buong pananagutan patuloy nating pagbubutihin

asr-000288
01:02:10.560 --> 01:02:17.440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ang pagpapatupad ng ating mga programa palakasin ang monitoring at accountability at itiyakin ang

asr-000289
01:02:17.440 --> 01:02:23.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: servisyo at suporta ng pamahalan ay tunay na nakakarating sa mga magsasaka manging isda at mga

asr-000290
01:02:23.200 --> 01:02:25.940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pamayanang higit na nangangailangan nito

asr-000291
01:02:26.640 --> 01:02:33.780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: honorable members the proposed 2027 budget is about more than funding government programs

asr-000292
01:02:33.780 --> 01:02:39.320
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: it's about deciding what kind of agriculture we want to build and what kind of future we want

asr-000293
01:02:39.320 --> 01:02:46.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: for the people who produce our food we want food security we must invest in people in the systems

asr-000294
01:02:46.200 --> 01:02:51.960
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: that make it possible if you want affordable food we must help farmers and fisher folks become more

asr-000295
01:02:51.960 --> 01:02:56.620
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: productive competitive and profitable and if you want a better life for all you need to

asr-000296
01:02:56.640 --> 01:03:00.940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: support our people we must also build a better life for those who feed the nation with the

asr-000297
01:03:00.940 --> 01:03:06.740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: continuous support of congress we can do more to modernize philippine agriculture strengthen our

asr-000298
01:03:06.740 --> 01:03:12.940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: fishery sector improve productivity incomes and build a food system that is more secure

asr-000299
01:03:12.940 --> 01:03:18.460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: resilient and responsive to the needs of a growing population this is not simply an investment in

asr-000300
01:03:18.460 --> 01:03:23.980
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: agriculture it is an investment in food security it is an investment in our farmers and fisher folks

