asr-000335
01:04:40.930 --> 01:04:44.110
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and situation of agriculture and fisheries sector

asr-000336
01:04:44.110 --> 01:04:47.530
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and the planning paradigms that guide the Department

asr-000337
01:04:47.530 --> 01:04:49.490
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: in its priority interventions.

asr-000338
01:04:50.310 --> 01:04:52.710
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This will provide the broader context

asr-000339
01:04:52.710 --> 01:04:56.090
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: for understanding on how our priorities

asr-000340
01:04:56.090 --> 01:05:00.390
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: are translated into programs, investments under the NEP.

asr-000341
01:05:01.070 --> 01:05:04.610
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: After this overview, Undersecretary Nora Olivares

asr-000342
01:05:04.610 --> 01:05:07.050
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: will walk us through the details

asr-000343
01:05:07.050 --> 01:05:09.050
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: of the National Expenditure Program.

asr-000344
01:05:09.810 --> 01:05:10.910
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: If I may proceed, Mr. Chair.

asr-000345
01:05:10.930 --> 01:05:33.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The PSA reported 3.1% growth in agriculture,

asr-000346
01:05:33.200 --> 01:05:38.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: forestry, and fisheries gross value added in 2025,

asr-000347
01:05:38.200 --> 01:05:43.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: rebounding from 1.5% contraction in 2024.

asr-000348
01:05:43.200 --> 01:05:50.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Despite this recovery, the long-term remains work-in-progress,

asr-000349
01:05:50.200 --> 01:05:52.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: as crops, livestock, and fisheries will continue to grow,

asr-000350
01:05:52.200 --> 01:05:53.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and farmers will continue to grow.

asr-000351
01:05:53.200 --> 01:05:54.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In addition,

asr-000352
01:05:54.200 --> 01:05:55.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: agriculture and fisheries have yet to return

asr-000353
01:05:55.200 --> 01:05:56.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: into their peak levels,

asr-000354
01:05:56.200 --> 01:05:59.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: leaving poultry the sole exception, with 9.1% growth.

asr-000355
01:05:59.200 --> 01:06:04.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Consequently, agriculture and fisheries' contribution

asr-000356
01:06:04.200 --> 01:06:12.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: to the overall economy fell to 7.9% in 2025,

asr-000357
01:06:12.200 --> 01:06:16.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: in contrast to the past growing sector.

asr-000358
01:06:16.200 --> 01:06:19.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000359
01:06:19.200 --> 01:06:21.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: But behind this number are our food producers,

asr-000360
01:06:21.200 --> 01:06:24.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: as of July 15, 2026,

asr-000361
01:06:24.200 --> 01:06:28.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the Registry System for Basic Sector in Agriculture,

asr-000362
01:06:28.200 --> 01:06:29.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: RSBSA,

asr-000363
01:06:29.200 --> 01:06:35.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: lists 10.44 million Munich individuals.

asr-000364
01:06:35.200 --> 01:06:39.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This aligns with PSA estimate that agriculture,

asr-000365
01:06:39.200 --> 01:06:44.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: fishery, and forestry employs around 10 million people,

asr-000366
01:06:44.200 --> 01:06:49.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: roughly 20%, or five in every one worker.

asr-000367
01:06:49.200 --> 01:06:50.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000368
01:06:51.200 --> 01:06:55.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The Registry highlights an aging workforce

asr-000369
01:06:55.200 --> 01:06:59.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: with an average age of 56 for farmers

asr-000370
01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:02.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and 51 for fisher folks,

asr-000371
01:07:02.200 --> 01:07:06.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: where 30% are 60% or older,

asr-000372
01:07:06.200 --> 01:07:11.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: or a mere 3% belongs to the agri-youth.

asr-000373
01:07:11.200 --> 01:07:13.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Addressing this dynamic requires supporting

asr-000374
01:07:13.200 --> 01:07:16.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: current registered stakeholders,

asr-000375
01:07:16.200 --> 01:07:19.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: while actively encouraging the younger generation

asr-000376
01:07:19.200 --> 01:07:21.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: to pursue

asr-000377
01:07:21.200 --> 01:07:23.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: their career in agriculture.

asr-000378
01:07:23.200 --> 01:07:26.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000379
01:07:26.730 --> 01:07:29.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The vast scale of people dependent on agriculture

asr-000380
01:07:29.730 --> 01:07:34.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and fisheries, alongside with its overall economic contribution,

asr-000381
01:07:34.730 --> 01:07:37.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: reveals a clear disparity.

asr-000382
01:07:37.730 --> 01:07:41.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: While 20% of the country's labor force is employed

asr-000383
01:07:41.730 --> 01:07:43.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: in agriculture and fishery,

asr-000384
01:07:43.730 --> 01:07:49.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the sector accounts only for 7.9% of the total GDP.

asr-000385
01:07:49.730 --> 01:07:51.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This imbalance,

asr-000386
01:07:51.730 --> 01:07:56.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: underscored a persistent gap between labor allocation

asr-000387
01:07:56.730 --> 01:07:58.730
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and economic productivity.

asr-000388
01:07:58.730 --> 01:08:01.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000389
01:08:01.080 --> 01:08:04.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Granular registry data further highlight

asr-000390
01:08:04.080 --> 01:08:07.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: this disparity across sub-sector,

asr-000391
01:08:07.080 --> 01:08:11.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: where gross value added relative to registered producer

asr-000392
01:08:11.080 --> 01:08:15.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: vary widely in relation to the commodity.

asr-000393
01:08:15.080 --> 01:08:17.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: For instance,

asr-000394
01:08:17.080 --> 01:08:21.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: coconut has the highest number of registered producers

asr-000395
01:08:21.080 --> 01:08:25.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: at approximately 3.05 million individuals,

asr-000396
01:08:25.080 --> 01:08:31.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: but the yield is only 82 billion in GBA.

asr-000397
01:08:31.080 --> 01:08:35.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Poultry presents a stark contrast,

asr-000398
01:08:35.080 --> 01:08:40.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: generating 225.59 billion in GBA

asr-000399
01:08:40.080 --> 01:08:43.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: from a far smaller workforce

asr-000400
01:08:43.080 --> 01:08:47.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: of 1.4 million registered producers.

asr-000401
01:08:47.080 --> 01:08:49.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Ultimately,

asr-000402
01:08:49.080 --> 01:08:52.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: this variation underscores why

asr-000403
01:08:52.080 --> 01:08:58.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: targeted policy planning must weigh in a unique scale,

asr-000404
01:08:58.080 --> 01:09:01.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: needs and output potential of each sub-sector.

asr-000405
01:09:01.080 --> 01:09:02.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: So,

asr-000406
01:09:02.080 --> 01:09:05.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: we think it should be targeted.

asr-000407
01:09:05.080 --> 01:09:07.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000408
01:09:07.080 --> 01:09:10.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Poverty among farmers and fisher folks

asr-000409
01:09:10.080 --> 01:09:15.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: has declined substantially over the past two decades.

asr-000410
01:09:15.080 --> 01:09:17.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Yet,

asr-000411
01:09:17.080 --> 01:09:22.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: it remains significantly higher than the national average.

asr-000412
01:09:22.080 --> 01:09:27.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This indicates that a wide overall macroeconomic progress

asr-000413
01:09:27.080 --> 01:09:29.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: has been achieved.

asr-000414
01:09:29.080 --> 01:09:34.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It has not yet translated fully into improved livelihood

asr-000415
01:09:34.080 --> 01:09:36.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: of those who depend on the sector,

asr-000416
01:09:36.080 --> 01:09:38.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: which, as the Secretary mentioned,

asr-000417
01:09:38.080 --> 01:09:41.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the ones who produce our food.

asr-000418
01:09:41.080 --> 01:09:44.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Closing this gap will require focused intervention

asr-000419
01:09:44.080 --> 01:09:46.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: to ensure growth directly reaches

asr-000420
01:09:46.080 --> 01:09:49.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the agricultural household.

asr-000421
01:09:49.080 --> 01:09:51.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000422
01:09:51.080 --> 01:09:54.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: As we have seen so far,

asr-000423
01:09:54.080 --> 01:09:58.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the agriculture and fishery sector creates value,

asr-000424
01:09:58.080 --> 01:10:00.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: yet food insecurity,

asr-000425
01:10:00.080 --> 01:10:05.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: poverty and vulnerability still persist.

asr-000426
01:10:05.080 --> 01:10:08.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000427
01:10:08.080 --> 01:10:11.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This persistent challenge

asr-000428
01:10:11.080 --> 01:10:14.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: can be traced to fundamental bottleneck

asr-000429
01:10:14.080 --> 01:10:15.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: across the agriculture

asr-000430
01:10:15.080 --> 01:10:18.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and fisheries value chain.

asr-000431
01:10:18.080 --> 01:10:21.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: With shrinking agricultural land,

asr-000432
01:10:21.080 --> 01:10:23.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: inadequate irrigation,

asr-000433
01:10:23.080 --> 01:10:25.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: high input costs,

asr-000434
01:10:25.080 --> 01:10:27.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: low mechanization

asr-000435
01:10:27.080 --> 01:10:32.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and increasing exposure to climate risk.

asr-000436
01:10:32.080 --> 01:10:34.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: At each stage,

asr-000437
01:10:34.080 --> 01:10:37.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: these constraints accumulate to add costs,

asr-000438
01:10:37.080 --> 01:10:39.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: reduce efficiency

asr-000439
01:10:39.080 --> 01:10:42.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and constrain overall productivity

asr-000440
01:10:42.080 --> 01:10:44.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and diminish

asr-000441
01:10:44.080 --> 01:10:46.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the profit and income

asr-000442
01:10:46.080 --> 01:10:48.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: of the farmers and fisher folks.

asr-000443
01:10:48.080 --> 01:10:50.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000444
01:10:50.080 --> 01:10:54.450
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Limited access to irrigation

asr-000445
01:10:54.450 --> 01:10:56.450
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and declining soil quality

asr-000446
01:10:56.450 --> 01:10:58.450
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: continue to restrain

asr-000447
01:10:58.450 --> 01:11:01.450
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the productive potential

asr-000448
01:11:01.450 --> 01:11:05.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: of our agricultural land.

asr-000449
01:11:05.080 --> 01:11:08.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Roughly 2.2 million hectares

asr-000450
01:11:08.080 --> 01:11:10.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: out of an estimated

asr-000451
01:11:10.080 --> 01:11:14.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: 3.13 million irrigable lands

asr-000452
01:11:14.080 --> 01:11:17.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: has been served,

asr-000453
01:11:17.330 --> 01:11:19.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: leaving 70% covered

asr-000454
01:11:19.330 --> 01:11:25.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and 29.75%

asr-000455
01:11:25.330 --> 01:11:28.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: is still requiring irrigation.

asr-000456
01:11:28.330 --> 01:11:31.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Soil health is equally concerning.

asr-000457
01:11:31.330 --> 01:11:33.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: With Bureau of Soils and Water Management data

asr-000458
01:11:33.330 --> 01:11:36.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: showing low to moderate productivity

asr-000459
01:11:36.330 --> 01:11:41.330
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: across 82% of rice and corn areas.

asr-000460
01:11:41.330 --> 01:11:44.220
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide.

asr-000461
01:11:44.220 --> 01:11:48.360
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000462
01:11:48.360 --> 01:11:52.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Okay.

asr-000463
01:11:52.800 --> 01:11:54.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Addressing this double challenge

asr-000464
01:11:54.800 --> 01:11:55.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: requires expanding

asr-000465
01:11:55.800 --> 01:11:57.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: irrigation infrastructure

asr-000466
01:11:57.800 --> 01:11:58.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: while strengthening

asr-000467
01:11:58.800 --> 01:12:01.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: targeted soil health intervention

asr-000468
01:12:01.800 --> 01:12:04.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: to unlock the land's productivity.

asr-000469
01:12:04.800 --> 01:12:08.620
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000470
01:12:08.620 --> 01:12:09.620
