asr-001046
01:51:22.040 --> 01:51:27.040
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and 2.39 billion for the communal irrigation systems.

asr-001047
01:51:27.040 --> 01:51:27.740
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: However,

asr-001048
01:51:28.600 --> 01:51:33.860
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: only 250 million was included in the FY2027 NEP.

asr-001049
01:51:34.360 --> 01:51:36.160
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The program aims to improve access

asr-001050
01:51:36.160 --> 01:51:38.520
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: to irrigation facilities and agricultural areas

asr-001051
01:51:38.520 --> 01:51:43.080
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: with proposed targets of 32.79 kilometers of gravel road

asr-001052
01:51:43.080 --> 01:51:46.160
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and 1.3 kilometers of concrete roads.

asr-001053
01:51:46.980 --> 01:51:49.220
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The repair program addresses deteriorated

asr-001054
01:51:49.220 --> 01:51:51.360
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and damaged canal structures and facilities

asr-001055
01:51:51.360 --> 01:51:53.520
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: that affect irrigation efficiency.

asr-001056
01:51:54.100 --> 01:51:56.680
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Its purpose is to restore operational,

asr-001057
01:51:57.040 --> 01:51:57.980
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: functionality,

asr-001058
01:51:58.340 --> 01:52:00.920
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and prevent further deterioration of existing systems.

asr-001059
01:52:01.580 --> 01:52:04.360
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: For the repair of irrigation systems,

asr-001060
01:52:04.540 --> 01:52:08.160
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: NEA proposed 38.26 billion

asr-001061
01:52:08.160 --> 01:52:10.600
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for the national irrigation system,

asr-001062
01:52:11.000 --> 01:52:15.880
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 20.52 billion for the communal irrigation system,

asr-001063
01:52:16.280 --> 01:52:20.180
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and 10.42 billion for the pump irrigation system,

asr-001064
01:52:20.580 --> 01:52:23.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: or around 70 billion lahat.

asr-001065
01:52:23.780 --> 01:52:24.160
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: However,

asr-001066
01:52:24.920 --> 01:52:26.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the FY2027 NEP provides

asr-001067
01:52:27.040 --> 01:52:32.820
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: only 2,920,000,000 and 3,000,000,000 respectively.

asr-001068
01:52:32.820 --> 01:52:34.900
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: These investments are intended

asr-001069
01:52:34.900 --> 01:52:36.960
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: to restore damaged facilities

asr-001070
01:52:36.960 --> 01:52:38.300
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and improve the reliability

asr-001071
01:52:38.300 --> 01:52:41.660
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and efficiency of irrigation services.

asr-001072
01:52:42.740 --> 01:52:45.840
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The restoration program focuses on irrigation systems

asr-001073
01:52:45.840 --> 01:52:48.460
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: that have become non-operational

asr-001074
01:52:48.460 --> 01:52:50.580
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: due to natural disasters,

asr-001075
01:52:51.020 --> 01:52:51.660
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: prolonged neglect,

asr-001076
01:52:51.800 --> 01:52:53.960
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and severe structural damage.

asr-001077
01:52:54.060 --> 01:52:56.980
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Its purpose is to establish irrigation services,

asr-001078
01:52:56.980 --> 01:53:00.720
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and recover productivity in agricultural areas.

asr-001079
01:53:00.860 --> 01:53:04.220
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: For the restoration of irrigation systems,

asr-001080
01:53:04.760 --> 01:53:08.160
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: NEA proposed 7.26 billion

asr-001081
01:53:08.160 --> 01:53:10.700
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for the national irrigation system,

asr-001082
01:53:11.240 --> 01:53:14.680
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 13 billion for the communal irrigation system,

asr-001083
01:53:14.800 --> 01:53:16.880
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: or a total of more than 20 billion.

asr-001084
01:53:17.320 --> 01:53:17.680
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: However,

asr-001085
01:53:18.580 --> 01:53:21.000
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the FY2027 NEP provides only

asr-001086
01:53:21.000 --> 01:53:25.580
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 1 billion and 250 million respectively.

asr-001087
01:53:25.580 --> 01:53:26.900
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The program aims

asr-001088
01:53:26.900 --> 01:53:30.640
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: to restore about 2,243 hectares

asr-001089
01:53:30.640 --> 01:53:32.640
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: of previously irrigated areas

asr-001090
01:53:32.640 --> 01:53:34.640
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and bring back into productive use.

asr-001091
01:53:35.940 --> 01:53:37.020
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The next major program

asr-001092
01:53:37.020 --> 01:53:39.060
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: is the Irrigation System Development Program

asr-001093
01:53:39.060 --> 01:53:41.820
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: which serves as NEA's primary strategy

asr-001094
01:53:41.820 --> 01:53:44.300
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for expanding irrigation coverage nationwide.

asr-001095
01:53:44.720 --> 01:53:48.960
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: This objective is to construct new irrigation systems

asr-001096
01:53:48.960 --> 01:53:53.280
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and provide reliable and sustainable water supply

asr-001097
01:53:53.280 --> 01:53:55.880
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: to agricultural lands that remain unirrigated.

asr-001098
01:53:55.880 --> 01:53:58.380
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: For the Irrigation System Development,

asr-001099
01:53:58.380 --> 01:54:01.060
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: NEA proposed 34.94 billion

asr-001100
01:54:01.060 --> 01:54:04.540
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for the new national irrigation system projects,

asr-001101
01:54:05.080 --> 01:54:08.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: or 11.8 billion for the small reservoir irrigation projects.

asr-001102
01:54:09.220 --> 01:54:09.520
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: However,

asr-001103
01:54:10.180 --> 01:54:12.980
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the FY2027 NEP provides only

asr-001104
01:54:12.980 --> 01:54:18.960
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 7.56 billion and 4.58 billion respectively.

asr-001105
01:54:19.420 --> 01:54:21.020
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: This project aims to develop

asr-001106
01:54:21.020 --> 01:54:24.480
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: new irrigation areas and expand irrigation coverage,

asr-001107
01:54:24.480 --> 01:54:25.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: which is proposed

asr-001108
01:54:25.800 --> 01:54:31.140
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: with a target of 1,226 hectares of new areas.

asr-001109
01:54:31.140 --> 01:54:34.180
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Priority projects under this program include

asr-001110
01:54:34.180 --> 01:54:37.180
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the ongoing Halaor River Multipurpose Project,

asr-001111
01:54:37.900 --> 01:54:40.400
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the Balog-Balog Multipurpose Project Phase 2,

asr-001112
01:54:40.940 --> 01:54:43.500
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the Ilocos Norte-Ilocosor Abray Irrigation Project,

asr-001113
01:54:43.780 --> 01:54:46.940
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and the Tomawini River Multipurpose Project,

asr-001114
01:54:47.220 --> 01:54:51.080
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: among other strategic irrigation infrastructure projects nationwide.

asr-001115
01:54:52.020 --> 01:54:55.520
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: This slide presents NEA's other major developments,

asr-001116
01:54:55.800 --> 01:54:57.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: including the development of new irrigation systems

asr-001117
01:54:57.800 --> 01:54:59.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and the development of new irrigation systems.

asr-001118
01:54:59.800 --> 01:55:01.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The project aims to expand irrigation coverage

asr-001119
01:55:01.800 --> 01:55:03.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: to upland, remote, and water-deficient areas

asr-001120
01:55:03.800 --> 01:55:06.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: where conventional gravity systems are not feasible,

asr-001121
01:55:06.800 --> 01:55:09.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: while also supporting agrarian reform beneficiaries.

asr-001122
01:55:09.800 --> 01:55:11.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: For FY2027,

asr-001123
01:55:11.800 --> 01:55:14.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: the NEP includes 7.92 billion

asr-001124
01:55:14.800 --> 01:55:16.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for the establishment of pump irrigation projects,

asr-001125
01:55:16.800 --> 01:55:22.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 4.58 billion for the special irrigation projects,

asr-001126
01:55:22.800 --> 01:55:24.800
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 200 million for the extension and expansion

asr-001127
01:55:24.800 --> 01:55:25.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: of existing irrigation systems,

asr-001128
01:55:25.780 --> 01:55:30.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and 698 million for the CARP-IC.

asr-001129
01:55:30.780 --> 01:55:33.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: These investments are expected to generate

asr-001130
01:55:33.780 --> 01:55:37.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: 4,160 hectares of new irrigated areas

asr-001131
01:55:37.780 --> 01:55:39.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and restore 531 hectares,

asr-001132
01:55:39.780 --> 01:55:42.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: thereby increasing agricultural productivity,

asr-001133
01:55:42.780 --> 01:55:44.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: improving water access,

asr-001134
01:55:44.780 --> 01:55:46.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and underserved communities,

asr-001135
01:55:46.780 --> 01:55:50.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and contributing to inclusive rural development.

asr-001136
01:55:50.780 --> 01:55:52.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: The National Irrigation Administration

asr-001137
01:55:52.780 --> 01:55:54.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: respectfully seeks the support

asr-001138
01:55:54.780 --> 01:55:56.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: of the House of Representatives

asr-001139
01:55:56.780 --> 01:56:00.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for an increase in NEA's FY2027 budget.

asr-001140
01:56:00.780 --> 01:56:02.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: This investment is essential

asr-001141
01:56:02.780 --> 01:56:04.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: to accelerate irrigation development,

asr-001142
01:56:04.780 --> 01:56:07.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: restore and rehabilitate existing systems,

asr-001143
01:56:07.780 --> 01:56:10.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: adapt climate-resilient technologies,

asr-001144
01:56:10.780 --> 01:56:13.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and contribute to countries' food security.

asr-001145
01:56:13.780 --> 01:56:14.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: With your continued support,

asr-001146
01:56:14.780 --> 01:56:17.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: NEA remains committed to providing efficient,

asr-001147
01:56:17.780 --> 01:56:20.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: sustainable, and resilient irrigation systems

asr-001148
01:56:20.780 --> 01:56:22.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: for our Filipino farmers.

asr-001149
01:56:22.780 --> 01:56:24.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Thank you very much,

asr-001150
01:56:24.780 --> 01:56:26.780
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and we are ready to respond to your questions.

asr-001151
01:56:26.780 --> 01:56:34.290
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you, Administrator Eddie Guillen.

asr-001152
01:56:34.290 --> 01:56:45.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: May I remind our distinguished colleagues

asr-001153
01:56:45.360 --> 01:56:50.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: that each member is allowed five minutes

asr-001154
01:56:50.360 --> 01:56:54.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: for questions or interpolation,

asr-001155
01:56:54.360 --> 01:56:59.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: excluding the responses of the resource persons.

asr-001156
01:56:59.360 --> 01:57:01.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: When the bell sounds,

asr-001157
01:57:01.360 --> 01:57:05.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the member has 30 seconds

asr-001158
01:57:05.360 --> 01:57:07.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: to conclude.

asr-001159
01:57:07.360 --> 01:57:09.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: And also,

asr-001160
01:57:09.360 --> 01:57:13.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: may I remind also my colleagues,

asr-001161
01:57:13.360 --> 01:57:17.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: there will be a consultation on Thursday,

asr-001162
01:57:17.360 --> 01:57:19.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: September 3,

asr-001163
01:57:19.360 --> 01:57:22.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: where your parochial concern

asr-001164
01:57:22.360 --> 01:57:26.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: may be addressed by the Department of Agriculture.

asr-001165
01:57:26.360 --> 01:57:29.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: So that we don't have to wait

asr-001166
01:57:29.360 --> 01:57:32.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: for the interpellation of the DA.

asr-001167
01:57:32.360 --> 01:57:34.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Please.

asr-001168
01:57:35.360 --> 01:57:39.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Consistent with the long-standing practice

asr-001169
01:57:39.360 --> 01:57:41.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: of the House,

asr-001170
01:57:41.360 --> 01:57:46.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the Chair shall recognize minority,

asr-001171
01:57:46.360 --> 01:57:49.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and then independent,

asr-001172
01:57:49.360 --> 01:57:51.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and majority members

asr-001173
01:57:51.360 --> 01:57:54.360
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: in an alternating manners

asr-001174
01:57:54.360 --> 01:58:07.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: when practicable.

asr-001175
01:58:07.340 --> 01:58:09.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The Chair first recognize

asr-001176
01:58:09.340 --> 01:58:17.720
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the Honorable Representative Sara Ilago.

asr-001177
01:58:17.720 --> 01:58:18.720
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Minority.

asr-001178
01:58:19.720 --> 01:58:20.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat

asr-001179
01:58:20.720 --> 01:58:22.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at magandang araw sa lahat.

asr-001180
01:58:22.720 --> 01:58:23.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair,

asr-001181
01:58:23.720 --> 01:58:25.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: dahil sa habagat at sunod-sunod na bagyo,

asr-001182
01:58:25.720 --> 01:58:28.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: tinatayang nasa 2.5 billion pesos

asr-001183
01:58:28.720 --> 01:58:29.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang agricultural damage.

asr-001184
01:58:29.720 --> 01:58:31.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sa presentation nga ng DA,

asr-001185
01:58:31.720 --> 01:58:34.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sinabi nila na yung estimated damage and losses

asr-001186
01:58:34.720 --> 01:58:37.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: from 2024 hanggang ngayong taon

asr-001187
01:58:37.720 --> 01:58:39.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay nasa 114 billion pesos

asr-001188
01:58:39.720 --> 01:58:41.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na nakaka-apekto sa halos 3 million

asr-001189
01:58:41.720 --> 01:58:43.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na mga magsasakat may ngisda.

asr-001190
01:58:43.720 --> 01:58:46.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ano po ang aksyon na ginagawa dito ng DA?

asr-001191
01:58:46.720 --> 01:58:47.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At paano makaka-apekto

asr-001192
01:58:47.720 --> 01:58:50.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: yung lubusan na pagkabawas ng inyong pondo

asr-001193
01:58:50.720 --> 01:58:52.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa 2027

asr-001194
01:58:52.720 --> 01:58:54.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sa madalian na aksyon natin

asr-001195
01:58:54.720 --> 01:58:58.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para tulungan ang mga affected farmers and fisherfolk?

asr-001196
01:58:58.720 --> 01:59:04.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair,

asr-001197
01:59:04.850 --> 01:59:06.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair,

asr-001198
01:59:06.850 --> 01:59:09.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: for next year, sa 2027,

asr-001199
01:59:09.850 --> 01:59:11.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: mas nakahanda kami, no?

asr-001200
01:59:11.850 --> 01:59:14.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Nakausap, nagpulong kami kahapon actually

asr-001201
01:59:14.850 --> 01:59:16.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: with the President,

asr-001202
01:59:16.850 --> 01:59:19.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: and doon yung DBM and other government agencies.

asr-001203
01:59:19.850 --> 01:59:20.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And,

asr-001204
01:59:20.850 --> 01:59:23.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pagdating sa mga tulong sa tao

asr-001205
01:59:23.850 --> 01:59:29.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: in terms of yung support sa immediate needs,

asr-001206
01:59:29.850 --> 01:59:33.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: parang may kanya-kanya na kaming assignment, no?

asr-001207
01:59:33.850 --> 01:59:36.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Basically, DSW will take care of yung immediate needs

asr-001208
01:59:36.850 --> 01:59:38.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: sa food and shelter.

asr-001209
01:59:38.850 --> 01:59:43.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: DOLE will take care of yung rehabilitation.

asr-001210
01:59:43.850 --> 01:59:46.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meanwhile, the DA,

asr-001211
01:59:46.850 --> 01:59:49.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: we are, bigyan ng budget kami, of course,

asr-001212
01:59:49.850 --> 01:59:53.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: sa QRF namin para mapabilis.

asr-001213
01:59:53.850 --> 01:59:56.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At nabigyan ng instruction ang DBM,

asr-001214
01:59:56.850 --> 01:59:59.850
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, na pag nangyari ganyan,

asr-001226
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:05.040
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: hindi na maghihintay ng mahabang panahon para ma-release yung Quick Response Fund.

asr-001227
02:00:05.140 --> 02:00:10.420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And basically, yung QRF namin will be used for yung replanting na tinatawag, no?

asr-001228
02:00:11.260 --> 02:00:15.740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pagdating sa seeds, tsaka yung abono na kailangan.

asr-001229
02:00:15.740 --> 02:00:22.160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But meanwhile, we're still trying to shorten yung sa indemnification payment ng PCIC,

asr-001230
02:00:22.160 --> 02:00:30.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: among others, tsaka yung mga loan programs na available like yung sa SURE natin for the affected areas, no?

asr-001231
02:00:31.940 --> 02:00:40.640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Of course, meron din taming, for this year, meron din kami na may na-allocate din sa amin ng dole na certain amount

asr-001232
02:00:40.640 --> 02:00:47.640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na pwede naming, lalo lang sa mga fisher folks na hindi makapaglaot dahil sa lakas ng habagat,

asr-001233
02:00:49.340 --> 02:00:52.100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: meron kaming, pwede kaming magbigay ng tupad konti.

asr-001234
02:00:52.160 --> 02:00:57.040
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Through dole, of course, no? Para doon sa mga, and others.

asr-001235
02:00:58.000 --> 02:01:06.180
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Then, doon sa El Niño response din, meron kami na may pasok na 6.7 billion na pondo ngayon

asr-001236
02:01:06.180 --> 02:01:12.640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: to be ready for the El Niño and that is one plus yung sa fuel issue.

asr-001237
02:01:12.640 --> 02:01:21.880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So, half of that will be for fuel subsidy and the other half will be for a transport subsidy.

asr-001238
02:01:21.880 --> 02:01:30.920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung para matulungan yung mga farmers and fisher folks na madala yung kanilang mga produkto at lower cost to the markets.

asr-001239
02:01:31.160 --> 02:01:32.220
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Among others, Mr. Chair.

asr-001240
02:01:33.120 --> 02:01:36.580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, may indemnification, meron din loans, no?

asr-001241
02:01:36.680 --> 02:01:43.020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero pagdating sa mga subsidies, meron ba kayong naging proposal para may direkta na production subsidy

asr-001242
02:01:43.020 --> 02:01:45.600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sa ating mga bumabangon na farmers at fisher folks?

asr-001243
02:01:45.820 --> 02:01:48.580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Na-mention nyo din po yung role dito ng DSWD.

asr-001244
02:01:48.580 --> 02:01:50.860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron na ba kayo ngayong figure?

asr-001245
02:01:51.200 --> 02:01:51.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kung magkano?

asr-001246
02:01:51.880 --> 02:01:56.220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: O yung nakalaan para sa calamity compensation sa affected farmers and fisher folks?

asr-001247
02:01:57.400 --> 02:02:04.580
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Well, sa 2027, the idea is through this package is about 10 billion din.

asr-001248
02:02:05.360 --> 02:02:09.860
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Which partly will be under presidential assistance for farmers and fisher folks.

asr-001249
02:02:10.240 --> 02:02:13.880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Plus yung QRF na pwede naming i-replenish, Mr. Chair.

asr-001250
02:02:14.860 --> 02:02:17.920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, yung presidential assistance kasi kulang na kulang.

asr-001251
02:02:18.260 --> 02:02:21.860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagdating sa production subsidy, may mga proposals dito sa House.

asr-001252
02:02:21.880 --> 02:02:25.980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Na 80,000 no kada magsasaka per cropping season.

asr-001253
02:02:26.200 --> 02:02:28.880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron din pong nasa 30 to 40,000 kada mangingisda.

asr-001254
02:02:29.700 --> 02:02:35.800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ayan, kaya yan po dapat ay sa DA na mismo manggaling na ang kailangan ng mga magsasaka at mangingisda.

asr-001255
02:02:36.120 --> 02:02:38.880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi po dagdag na pa-utang, kundi dagdag na direkta ang subsidiya.

asr-001256
02:02:39.840 --> 02:02:45.940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Mr. Chair, nais ko pong magtanong dun sa mga pagkakataon na napipilitang magtapon, magsira,

asr-001257
02:02:46.100 --> 02:02:48.340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: o iwan ng mga magsasaka yung kanilang ani.

asr-001258
02:02:48.600 --> 02:02:50.100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil wala pong bumibili.

asr-001259
02:02:50.920 --> 02:02:51.740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil napakababa.

asr-001260
02:02:51.880 --> 02:02:55.260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: O dahil kulang na kulang ang storage facilities.

asr-001261
02:02:55.400 --> 02:02:58.760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At mahal din yung gastos pagdating sa logistics.

asr-001262
02:02:59.140 --> 02:03:02.760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Lalo na po nitong pagsirit ng presyo ng langis.

asr-001263
02:03:03.440 --> 02:03:07.860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ilan po ba ang documented cases ng Department of Agriculture tungkol dito?

asr-001264
02:03:08.200 --> 02:03:14.680
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At meron ba kayong naging mekanismo para naman humaisal ba itong mga produkto ng ating mga magsasaka?

asr-001265
02:03:15.680 --> 02:03:21.680
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, well recognized niyong ating mga proponente.

asr-001266
02:03:21.880 --> 02:03:30.820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang problema sa, like recently dito sa Habagat, tumuhumal ang benta sa mga merkado sa ating mga palengke.

asr-001267
02:03:31.000 --> 02:03:37.140
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Kaya medyo tumuhumal din yung bentahan ng high value crops galing sa Benguet.

asr-001268
02:03:37.140 --> 02:03:50.820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At ang nadesisyon na ito actually earlier this year na magtatayo tayo ng cold storage na 5 mega cold storage

asr-001269
02:03:50.820 --> 02:03:56.300
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at processing center dun sa lupa ng Benguet State University

asr-001270
02:03:56.300 --> 02:04:06.460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: as one of the solutions to have a 15 day buffer stocking area and processing for yung mga excess production natin.

asr-001271
02:04:07.140 --> 02:04:16.120
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meanwhile, meron din tayong food hub na ipapabid na sa Clark with the 2026 gaan na 2 billion pesos

asr-001272
02:04:16.120 --> 02:04:19.380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: by next, ah this month, September, no?

asr-001273
02:04:19.380 --> 02:04:20.700
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So that will be completed.

asr-001274
02:04:20.820 --> 02:04:27.820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So that will be complimentary plus yung tinatapos natin na FTI na 500 million na mega cold storage sa Taguig.

asr-001275
02:04:28.320 --> 02:04:32.740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So that is part of the network na tinatayo natin for the high value crops.

asr-001276
02:04:33.160 --> 02:04:42.940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At para nga meron tayong shock absorber at storage systems to address yung spikes or highs and lows ng production.

asr-001277
02:04:42.940 --> 02:04:50.700
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And of course, pati yung mga weather to address yung effects nito sa mga weather disturbances din.

asr-001278
02:04:50.820 --> 02:04:54.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So that we will have market stability among others.

asr-001279
02:04:54.300 --> 02:04:54.820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ah, Mr. Chair.

asr-001280
02:04:55.500 --> 02:05:05.040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, hingin po natin yung ulat ng DA pagdating dito sa pagpapayaman ng ating tulong pagdating sa logistics chain natin sa pagkain.

asr-001281
02:05:05.560 --> 02:05:07.820
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At dagdag na rin po yung matagal na nating panawagan.

asr-001282
02:05:08.540 --> 02:05:14.160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sana naman yung DA na rin yung manguna sa pagtatanggal ng VAT at excise tax sa langis.

asr-001283
02:05:14.440 --> 02:05:18.320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil kayo mismo yung pinaka nakakaalam, di ba?

asr-001284
02:05:18.320 --> 02:05:20.320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kung gaano po kailangan-kailangan ng mga magsasakal.

asr-001285
02:05:20.820 --> 02:05:23.960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At may isda ang krudo pagdating sa kanilang produksyon.

asr-001286
02:05:24.320 --> 02:05:30.280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Mr. Chair, nananatili pa rin ho ang Pilipinas na number one na rice importer sa buong mundo.

asr-001287
02:05:31.040 --> 02:05:40.940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sa harap ngayon ng bantanang super-aluminium, climate emergency, mga gera, at mga potential na disruption sa ating global rice supply.

asr-001288
02:05:40.940 --> 02:05:50.700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi ba delikado para sa ating food security na ang Pilipinas po ang laki pa rin ng pag-asa ng kanyang dependence sa ibang bansa para sa ating panggawa?

asr-001289
02:05:50.820 --> 02:05:54.220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ano na yung pagkain? Ano ho ang aksyon ng DA para rito?

asr-001290
02:05:54.440 --> 02:06:00.740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, definitely, ang pangarap po natin ay mabawasan yung ating dependency sa importasyon.

asr-001291
02:06:01.600 --> 02:06:13.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At napaka-importante hung ma-suportahan natin ang NIA sa pag-irrigate ng more of our flatlands na tinatawag, lalo na sa rice production.

asr-001292
02:06:14.640 --> 02:06:19.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meanwhile, tuloy-tuloy naman yung ating development of the...

asr-001293
02:06:19.060 --> 02:06:26.820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: for use ng ating development ng inbred seeds natin at pati yung locally produced hybrid seeds natin.

asr-001294
02:06:27.080 --> 02:06:33.700
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At actually, unting-unting tumataas ang ating yield per hectare base sa datos.

asr-001295
02:06:34.380 --> 02:06:38.520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So, we're in the right path but we really need more irrigated land.

asr-001296
02:06:38.520 --> 02:06:49.040
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: As far as food security natin for rice for year 2026, I'm happy to announce na we are quite secure.

asr-001297
02:06:49.060 --> 02:06:53.300
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa ating rice requirements till end of 2026.

asr-001298
02:06:54.920 --> 02:06:58.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At that is because yung...

asr-001299
02:06:58.980 --> 02:07:05.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: As of last week, 3.8 million tons na ang na-import ng ating bansa dahil ito ay liberalized.

asr-001300
02:07:06.320 --> 02:07:13.900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But pumasok na rin ho, nag-umpisa na ho ang harvest season din natin ngayon sa ating mga palayan.

asr-001301
02:07:13.900 --> 02:07:17.420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Like sa sarili kong farm sa Nueva Ecija, nag-harvest na last week.

asr-001302
02:07:17.940 --> 02:07:19.040
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So far, maayos naman.

asr-001303
02:07:19.060 --> 02:07:25.460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At of course, it can be better sana but then basang-basa kasi palay.

asr-001304
02:07:25.680 --> 02:07:34.080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero we are seeing na although may tama tayo na about 60,000 hectares as of yesterday,

asr-001305
02:07:34.880 --> 02:07:42.620
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: but mukhang maayos pa rin yung harvest natin itong harvest season na to.

asr-001306
02:07:42.720 --> 02:07:45.360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So that should carry us over until end of the year.

asr-001307
02:07:45.540 --> 02:07:46.080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair.

asr-001308
02:07:46.080 --> 02:07:48.980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, hindi lang sa bigas mataas ang ating food importation.

asr-001309
02:07:49.060 --> 02:07:56.600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kung sa taon 1990 hanggang 2022, ang bigas po lumaki ng from 9 to 23 percent.

asr-001310
02:07:56.960 --> 02:07:59.480
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa mais, 6.7 to 10.1 percent.

asr-001311
02:07:59.900 --> 02:08:02.180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa beef, 8.5 to 50 percent.

asr-001312
02:08:02.520 --> 02:08:04.920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa pork, 0.1 to 30.4 percent.

asr-001313
02:08:05.080 --> 02:08:07.240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Chicken, 0.1 to 11.9.

asr-001314
02:08:07.300 --> 02:08:13.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sa galunggong po, maski galunggong, ang taas po ng ating import dependence na ngayon ay nasa 23.4 percent.

asr-001315
02:08:13.720 --> 02:08:18.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa DA na mismo nang galing po last year, Mr. Chair, na hindi po para sa Pilipinas ang liberalization.

asr-001316
02:08:19.060 --> 02:08:20.360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang full liberalization.

asr-001317
02:08:21.320 --> 02:08:29.000
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya ang dapat yung budget natin ay sumunod din doon sa kagustuhan natin na mabaliktad yung liberalization ng agriculture.

asr-001318
02:08:29.360 --> 02:08:35.080
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero ang nakikita po natin ngayon sa budget, puro budget cut po ang national rice program, national corn program.

asr-001319
02:08:35.400 --> 02:08:42.500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Paano po natin maabot ang pagpapayaman ng lokal na agrikultura kung puro budget cut ang nakita natin ngayon sa sektor na agrikultura?

asr-001320
02:08:42.940 --> 02:08:48.500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Mr. Chair, tungkol po sa mga agricultural products,

asr-001321
02:08:49.060 --> 02:08:51.200
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: lands na maaari po na maapektuhan

asr-001322
02:08:51.200 --> 02:08:52.880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng Pax Silica Initiative?

asr-001323
